[{"tag_name":"b12377","prerelease":true,"created_at":"2026-11-14T08:49:27Z","body":"<details open>\n\nspec + model: refactor DFlash based speculative decoding methods  (#32016)\n\n* dflash : move the DSpark markov head and backbone graphs to dspark.cpp\n\nMove-only: build_dspark_markov_head, graph_dsv4, graph_dsv41 and\ngraph_mistral_large4 move verbatim. build_inp_target_features and\nbuild_dspark_markov_head become static members of llama_model_dflash so\nboth files can use them.\n\n* dflash : detect the head and the backbone once, split the loaders per file\n\nload_arch_hparams sets llama_model_dflash::variant (DFlash, DFlash2,\nDSpark, LiliCorr) and ::backbone (base, DSV4, DSV4.1, Mistral Large 4).\nThe head, backbone and base layer loaders become member helpers in\ndflash.cpp, dflash2.cpp, lilicorr.cpp and dspark.cpp. build_arch_graph\ndispatches on the backbone.\n\nThe DFlash2 and LiliCorr loaders create the DFlash2 conv tensors through\na helper in dflash2.cpp, right after their head tensors instead of in\nthe base layer loop; the other tensors keep their creation order. The\nDFlash2 loader drops its copy of the conv group size check, which master\nnever reached.\n\n* dflash : share the injection input, token embeddings and lm head lookups\n\nbuild_inject_inp (target features + fc + encoder norm), get_tok_embd and\nget_lm_head replace the copies in the base, DSV4, DSV4.1 and Mistral\nLarge 4 graphs. build_inp_target_features is file-static again.\n\n* dflash : split the DFlash decoder into a graph per head\n\ngraph_base creates the shared inputs and provides build_inject,\nbuild_inp_tokens, build_layers and build_logits. graph_dflash\n(dflash.cpp), graph_dflash2 (dflash2.cpp), graph_dspark (dspark.cpp) and\ngraph_lilicorr (lilicorr.cpp) assemble them and add their head; the\nselector, scorer and markov head builders move to the file of their\ngraph, and the DFlash2 local conv run by build_layers to dflash2.cpp.\nbuild_arch_graph dispatches on the backbone, then on the head.\n\nThe op order and the tensor names are unchanged.\n\n* speculative : split the DFlash driver into a class per head\n\ncommon_speculative_impl_draft_dflash stays the DFlash implementation and\nbecomes the base of draft_dspark, draft_dflash2 and draft_lilicorr. Its\nprotected constructor only reads the draft metadata; init() then sets up\nthe contexts with the options of the draft (draft length, backend\nsampling, device features, masked h_nextn). Each derived class overrides\ndraft() with the path of its head from the former draft(). DFlash2 also\noverrides begin() to reseed its generator per request, and LiliCorr\noverrides process() to store the context features of each injected\nchunk, which its noise block carries as its state.\n\nThe factory keeps the current routing: draft-dspark picks DSpark,\ndraft-dflash picks DFlash2 or LiliCorr from the draft metadata and\nDFlash otherwise. draft-dspark with a DFlash2 or LiliCorr draft now runs\nthe DSpark reader instead of a mix of both. sample_from_anchor is logged\nby DSpark only.\n\n* speculative : add the draft-dflash2 and draft-lilicorr types\n\ndraft-dflash2 and draft-lilicorr name the DFlash2 and LiliCorr drafts,\nwhich draft-dflash keeps running too: it picks them from the draft\nmetadata. draft-dflash2 and draft-lilicorr must match the draft model,\ndraft-dspark rejects a DFlash2 or LiliCorr draft, a model that is not a\nDFlash draft is rejected, and a run uses at most one DFlash family type;\nthese errors leave speculative decoding uninitialized.\n\nThe type detected from the draft GGUF is now the concrete one, and\ndraft-dflash2 and draft-lilicorr download the dflash sidecar.\n\n* docs : describe the DFlash2 and LiliCorr drafts\n\nAdd the DFlash2 and LiliCorr sections and the new types, and explain\nthat draft-dflash also runs DFlash2 and LiliCorr drafts.\n\n* speculative : drop the unused DFlash is_mrope\n\nNothing reads it since the migration to common_batch (#29385), which\npicks the number of M-RoPE position rows from the rope type of the draft.\n\n* doc: update spec dec\n\n* address review comments\n\n</details>\n\n**Website:**\n- <https://llama.app>\n\n**Attestations:**\n- <https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/attestations/67506529>\n\n**macOS/iOS:**\n- [macOS Apple Silicon (arm64)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12377/llama-b12377-bin-macos-arm64.tar.gz)\n- macOS Apple Silicon (arm64, KleidiAI enabled) [DISABLED](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/23780)\n- [macOS Intel (x64)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12377/llama-b12377-bin-macos-x64.tar.gz)\n- [iOS XCFramework](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12377/llama-b12377-xcframework.zip)\n\n**Linux:**\n- [Ubuntu x64 (CPU)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12377/llama-b12377-bin-ubuntu-x64.tar.gz)\n- [Ubuntu arm64 (CPU)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12377/llama-b12377-bin-ubuntu-arm64.tar.gz)\n- [Ubuntu 24.04 s390x (CPU)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12377/llama-b12377-bin-ubuntu-s390x.tar.gz)\n- [Ubuntu 26.04 s390x (CPU)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12377/llama-b12377-bin-ubuntu-26.04-s390x.tar.gz)\n- [Ubuntu 26.04 s390x (zDNN)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12377/llama-b12377-bin-ubuntu-zdnn-s390x.tar.gz)\n- [Ubuntu x64 (Vulkan)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12377/llama-b12377-bin-ubuntu-vulkan-x64.tar.gz)\n- [Ubuntu arm64 (Vulkan)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12377/llama-b12377-bin-ubuntu-vulkan-arm64.tar.gz)\n- [Ubuntu x64 (CUDA 12)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12377/llama-b12377-bin-ubuntu-cuda-12.8-x64.tar.gz) - [CUDA 12.8 libraries](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12377/cudart-llama-b12377-bin-ubuntu-cuda-12.8-x64.tar.gz)\n- [Ubuntu x64 (CUDA 13)](https://github.com/g