in cutoff\ndropped draft tokens the target would have accepted. Skip it when\nMTP or DFlash2 samples the draft. draft-simple keeps it: each extra\ndraft token costs a full draft model pass.\n\n* spec : replace the sampled-draft p_min skip with a warning\n\np_min behaves as on master again for every drafter and sampling mode.\nInstead, log a warning when --spec-draft-p-min > 0 is used with\n--spec-draft-sampling probabilistic, suggesting p_min 0: under\nrejection sampling the draft's top probability does not tell how much\nof the draft the target accepts. The cut is not skipped because with\nMTP at long drafts it can still pay off.\n\n* spec : warn about p_min only for drafters that use it\n\nThe n-gram drafters ignore p_min, and DSpark uses it as the cutoff of its confidence head, so the warning is skipped when only these are configured.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Pranesh Gonegandla <pgonegandla@nvidia.com>\n\n</details>\n\n**Website:**\n- <https://llama.app>\n\n**Attestations:**\n- <https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/attestations/67303781>\n\n**macOS/iOS:**\n- [macOS Apple Silicon (arm64)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12364/llama-b12364-bin-macos-arm64.tar.gz)\n- macOS Apple Silicon (arm64, KleidiAI enabled) [DISABLED](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/23780)\n- [macOS Intel (x64)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12364/llama-b12364-bin-macos-x64.tar.gz)\n- [iOS XCFramework](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12364/llama-b12364-xcframework.zip)\n\n**Linux:**\n- [Ubuntu x64 (CPU)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12364/llama-b12364-bin-ubuntu-x64.tar.gz)\n- [Ubuntu arm64 (CPU)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12364/llama-b12364-bin-ubuntu-arm64.tar.gz)\n- [Ubuntu 24.04 s390x (CPU)](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b12364/llama-b12364-bin-ubuntu-s390x.tar.gz)\n- [Ubuntu 26.04 s390x (CPU)](https://github.com